<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Máel Sechnaill mac Máele Ruanaid</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 862</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Máel Sechnaill I, Malachy I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Máel Sechnaill mac Máele Ruanaid was king of Mide and, from 846, high king of Ireland, of the Clann Cholmáin. He fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a>, drowning their leader Turgesius in 845, and he was the first high king to obtain the submission of most Irish provinces, including Munster. He died in 862.</p></div>
